{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RdJdCARVXeb7jrq3qU2FnR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Insights from Negative Results in NLP EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"CFP | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2021/cfp/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Insights 2024 | Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/proceedings/10.5555/1613715\"},{\"title\":\"2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Call For Papers: The Second Workshop on Insights from Negative Results (EMNLP 2021) | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/call-papers-second-workshop-insights-negative-results-emnlp-2021-0\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about \"Insights from Negative Results in NLP\" and EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 and Negative Results\n\nEMNLP 2026 has a goal of curating a diverse technical program—in addition to traditional research results, papers may contribute negative findings, survey an area, announce the creation of a new resource, argue a position, report novel linguistic insights derived using existing computational techniques, and reproduce (or fail to reproduce) previous results.\n\n## Insights from Negative Results Workshop\n\nThe \"Insights from Negative Results in NLP\" is an established workshop in the NLP community. Publication of negative results is difficult in most fields, but in NLP the problem is exacerbated by the near-universal focus on improvements in benchmarks. This situation implicitly discourages hypothesis-driven research, and it turns creation and fine-tuning of NLP models into art rather than science. Furthermore, it increases the time, effort, and carbon emissions spent on developing and tuning models, as the researchers have no opportunity to learn what has already been tried and failed.\n\nThe workshop invites both practical and theoretical unexpected or negative results that have important implications for future research, highlight methodological issues with existing approaches, and/or point out pervasive misunderstandings or bad practices.\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nWhile I found general ARR (ACL Rolling Review) reviewer guidelines and EMNLP reviewing advice, I did not find specific EMNLP 2026 reviewer form or review form details in the search results. The EMNLP 2026 papers use the ACL Rolling Review system, but detailed review form specifications may be available on the official EMNLP 2026 or ARR websites.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a93e6455-f184-4ae1-aabe-3c851fdec0e9","uuid":"e45f9d42-0e79-4675-b2d0-3b34d95d8a47","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:03:40.485Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Insights from Negative Results in NLP EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KT94t7WuaZm3SsGizmLSRG","content":[{"title":"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"CFP | Insights 2024","url":"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2021/cfp/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Insights 2024 | Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP","url":"https://insights-workshop.github.io/"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...","url":"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/proceedings/10.5555/1613715"},{"title":"2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Call For Papers: The Second Workshop on Insights from Negative Results (EMNLP 2021) | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/call-papers-second-workshop-insights-negative-results-emnlp-2021-0"}]},"Based on the web search results, here's what I found about \"Insights from Negative Results in NLP\" and EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 and Negative Results\n\nEMNLP 2026 has a goal of curating a diverse technical program—in addition to traditional research results, papers may contribute negative findings, survey an area, announce the creation of a new resource, argue a position, report novel linguistic insights derived using existing computational techniques, and reproduce (or fail to reproduce) previous results.\n\n## Insights from Negative Results Workshop\n\nThe \"Insights from Negative Results in NLP\" is an established workshop in the NLP community. Publication of negative results is difficult in most fields, but in NLP the problem is exacerbated by the near-universal focus on improvements in benchmarks. This situation implicitly discourages hypothesis-driven research, and it turns creation and fine-tuning of NLP models into art rather than science. Furthermore, it increases the time, effort, and carbon emissions spent on developing and tuning models, as the researchers have no opportunity to learn what has already been tried and failed.\n\nThe workshop invites both practical and theoretical unexpected or negative results that have important implications for future research, highlight methodological issues with existing approaches, and/or point out pervasive misunderstandings or bad practices.\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nWhile I found general ARR (ACL Rolling Review) reviewer guidelines and EMNLP reviewing advice, I did not find specific EMNLP 2026 reviewer form or review form details in the search results. The EMNLP 2026 papers use the ACL Rolling Review system, but detailed review form specifications may be available on the official EMNLP 2026 or ARR websites."],"durationSeconds":7.554579222999997}}
