ond Workshop on Insights from Negative Results (EMNLP 2021) | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/call-papers-second-workshop-insights-negative-results-emnlp-2021\"},{\"title\":\"Call for workshops: EMNLP & AACL\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/ml-news/c/W-fucfhVto4\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"}]\n\nLet me search specifically for the 2026 Insights workshop call for papers with more details:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Insights 2024 | Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"CFP | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2021/cfp/\"},{\"title\":\"Accepted papers | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/accepted/\"},{\"title\":\"Program - Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2022/program/\"},{\"title\":\"Organization | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2024/organization/\"},{\"title\":\"Program | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2023/program/\"},{\"title\":\"2020 | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2020/\"},{\"title\":\"PC | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2024/pc/\"}]\n\nLet me search for the 2026 workshop call for papers details:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CFP | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2021/cfp/\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"The Third Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/third-workshop-insights-negative-results-nlp-0\"},{\"title\":\"Insights 2024 | Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"[2nd CFP] Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP (@ACL 2022) - deadline Feb 28\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/ml-news/c/Hg3CbVFAgp4\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Track Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/CallForEvaluationsDatasets\"},{\"title\":\"The Third Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://aclweb.org/portal/content/third-workshop-insights-negative-results-nlp\"},{\"title\":\"Workshop on Insights from Negative Results | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/workshop-insights-negative-results\"},{\"title\":\"Insights 2024 : Fifth Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP\",\"url\":\"http://wikicfp.com/cfp/servlet/event.showcfp?eventid=178569\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I found information about the Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP that will be held at EMNLP 2026. Here's what I found:\n\n## Workshop Details\n\nThe Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP will be held in Budapest, Hungary, October 22-29, 2026 (co-located with EMNLP).\n\n## Workshop Focus\n\nThe workshop addresses the problem that publication of negative results is difficult in most fields, but in NLP the problem is exacerbated by the near-universal focus on improvements in benchmarks. This situation implicitly discourages hypothesis-driven research, and it turns creation and fine-tuning of NLP models into art rather than science. The workshop invites both practical and theoretical unexpected or negative results that have important implications for future research, highlight methodological issues with existing approaches, and/or point out pervasive misunderstandings or bad practices.\n\n## Types of Submissions\n\nBased on information from previous editions, the workshop accepts short papers (up to 4 pages, excluding references), as well as 1-2 page non-archival abstract submissions for papers published elsewhere (e.g. in one of the main conferences or in non-NLP venues).\n\n## Examples of Successful Submissions\n\nA successful negative results paper would contribute experiments on (in)stability of the previously published results due to hardware, random initializations, etc.; ablation studies of components in previously proposed models, showing that their contributions are different from the initially reported; datasets or probing tasks showing that previous approaches do not generalize to other domains or language phenomena; extensions or annotations of existing datasets which show that prior successes are due to spurious statistical factors or annotation artifacts; the respective contributions of pre-training vs fine-tuning to the end result; cross-lingual studies showing that a technique X is only successful for a certain language or language family.\n\n## Key Reviewer and Ethics Criteria\n\nEMNLP workshops follow the conference guidelines for honouring the ACM Code of Ethics, and per conference guidelines, a paper that may raise ethical issues needs to explicitly discuss them, and that discussion will be taken into account in the review process.\n\nFor specific details about the 2026 call for papers, reviewer criteria, and submission deadlines, I recommend visiting the workshop website at insights-workshop.github.io, which lists Call for papers, Accepted papers, Program, Sponsors, Organization, Invited Speakers, and Program Committee information.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a93e6455-f184-4ae1-aabe-3c851fdec0e9","uuid":"cb3de4d8-adfe-408b-be83-944cb94c38a5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:03:54.131Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"\"Insights from Negative Results in NLP\" workshop EMNLP 