{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D5nWSnDuRZ9FRiycf5hsZx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"insights-workshop.github.io 2025 2026 call for papers review criteria scoring\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - jiahaoli57/Call-for-Reviewers: This project aims to collect the latest \\\"call for reviewers\\\" links from various top CS/ML/AI conferences/journals · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jiahaoli57/Call-for-Reviewers\"},{\"title\":\"CFP | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/cfp/\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers - NeusymBridge Workshop\",\"url\":\"https://neusymbridge.github.io/call-for-papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Accepted papers | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/accepted/\"},{\"title\":\"Program | Insights 2024\",\"url\":\"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/program/\"},{\"title\":\"Main Technical Track: Call for Papers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/main-technical-track-call/\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers | Foundation Models for Structured Data\",\"url\":\"https://icml-structured-fm-workshop.github.io/call-for-papers/\"},{\"title\":\"EMR Workshop @ ECCV 2026\",\"url\":\"https://emr-workshop.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Research Papers\",\"url\":\"https://icde2026.github.io/cf-research-papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers - ICKG 2026\",\"url\":\"https://ickg2026.github.io/call-for-papers.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the Insights Workshop. However, the specific page about review criteria and scoring is not fully detailed in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\nThe Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP will be held in Albuquerque, New Mexico, May 2025 (co-located with NAACL).\n\nRegarding the call for papers, the workshop will run its own review process, and papers can be submitted directly to the workshop by March 10, 2024, or a paper accompanied with reviews from the ACL Rolling Review system can be submitted by April 7, 2024.\n\nThe search results show the Insights Workshop website (insights-workshop.github.io), but the specific details about review criteria and scoring rubrics are not included in the returned content. To get the complete information about their 2025/2026 review criteria and scoring guidelines, you would need to visit the actual workshop website directly at https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/cfp/ where this information may be more detailed.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a93e6455-f184-4ae1-aabe-3c851fdec0e9","uuid":"0c896ed3-6e57-4610-9fa3-cb67c4c2ef83","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:04:05.905Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"insights-workshop.github.io 2025 2026 call for papers review criteria scoring","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AyUpzfnHTe21vneQaXJiHC","content":[{"title":"GitHub - jiahaoli57/Call-for-Reviewers: This project aims to collect the latest \"call for reviewers\" links from various top CS/ML/AI conferences/journals · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/jiahaoli57/Call-for-Reviewers"},{"title":"CFP | Insights 2024","url":"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/cfp/"},{"title":"Call for Papers - NeusymBridge Workshop","url":"https://neusymbridge.github.io/call-for-papers.html"},{"title":"Accepted papers | Insights 2024","url":"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/accepted/"},{"title":"Program | Insights 2024","url":"https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/program/"},{"title":"Main Technical Track: Call for Papers - AAAI","url":"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/main-technical-track-call/"},{"title":"Call for Papers | Foundation Models for Structured Data","url":"https://icml-structured-fm-workshop.github.io/call-for-papers/"},{"title":"EMR Workshop @ ECCV 2026","url":"https://emr-workshop.github.io/"},{"title":"Research Papers","url":"https://icde2026.github.io/cf-research-papers.html"},{"title":"Call for Papers - ICKG 2026","url":"https://ickg2026.github.io/call-for-papers.html"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the Insights Workshop. However, the specific page about review criteria and scoring is not fully detailed in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\nThe Workshop on Insights from Negative Results in NLP will be held in Albuquerque, New Mexico, May 2025 (co-located with NAACL).\n\nRegarding the call for papers, the workshop will run its own review process, and papers can be submitted directly to the workshop by March 10, 2024, or a paper accompanied with reviews from the ACL Rolling Review system can be submitted by April 7, 2024.\n\nThe search results show the Insights Workshop website (insights-workshop.github.io), but the specific details about review criteria and scoring rubrics are not included in the returned content. To get the complete information about their 2025/2026 review criteria and scoring guidelines, you would need to visit the actual workshop website directly at https://insights-workshop.github.io/2025/cfp/ where this information may be more detailed."],"durationSeconds":5.867956578000005}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SHthEdcNjEqZGAG1vz7mb4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review reviewer form 2025 2026 scoring scale overall assessment soundness\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) reviewer form. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Scoring Scale and Assessment Components\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Assessment\n\nReviewers evaluate whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and for experimental papers, they consider the depth and/or breadth of the research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\nThe soundness scoring includes: 5 = Excellent (the study is one of the most thorough), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nThe overall recommendation scale includes: 5 = Consider for Award, 2 = Resubmit next cycle (substantial revisions that can be completed by the next ARR cycle), 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (substantial revisions that cannot be completed by the next ARR cycle), and 1 = Do not resubmit.\n\n## Important Guideline\n\nSoundness scores must be justified by the text of the review, and if you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a93e6455-f184-4ae1-aabe-3c851fdec0e9","uuid":"86c77923-5f5e-4908-9925-451e2f8fd2c5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:04:06.407Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review reviewer form 2025 2026 scoring scale overall assessment soundness","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015T6Wr7CJJzEjgvViCHYHxb","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"ARR Changelog – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"}]},"I found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) reviewer form. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Scoring Scale and Assessment Components\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Assessment\n\nReviewers evaluate whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and for experimental papers, they consider the depth and/or breadth of the research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\nThe soundness scoring includes: 5 = Excellent (the study is one of the most thorough), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nThe overall recommendation scale includes: 5 = Consider for Award, 2 = Resubmit next cycle (substantial revisions that can be completed by the next ARR cycle), 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (substantial revisions that cannot be completed by the next ARR cycle), and 1 = Do not resubmit.\n\n## Important Guideline\n\nSoundness scores must be justified by the text of the review, and if you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation."],"durationSeconds":6.806990424999996}}
